Note: the n-body simulation of the outer planets, as in the Computer Language Benchmarks Game.

a body has an x, a y, a z, a vx, a vy, a vz and a mass (decimal).
set sunmass to 4 times pi times pi.
set days to 365.24.

set bodies to an empty list.
add a new body with mass sunmass to bodies.
add a new body with x 4.84143144246472090, y -1.16032004402742839, z -0.103622044471123109,
  vx 0.00166007664274403694 times days, vy 0.00769901118419740425 times days,
  vz -0.0000690460016972063023 times days and mass 0.000954791938424326609 times sunmass to bodies.
add a new body with x 8.34336671824457987, y 4.12479856412430479, z -0.403523417114321381,
  vx -0.00276742510726862411 times days, vy 0.00499852801234917238 times days,
  vz 0.0000230417297573763929 times days and mass 0.000285885980666130812 times sunmass to bodies.
add a new body with x 12.8943695621391310, y -15.1111514016986312, z -0.223307578892655734,
  vx 0.00296460137564761618 times days, vy 0.00237847173959480950 times days,
  vz -0.0000296589568540237556 times days and mass 0.0000436624404335156298 times sunmass to bodies.
add a new body with x 15.3796971148509165, y -25.9193146099879641, z 0.179258772950371181,
  vx 0.00268067772490389322 times days, vy 0.00162824170038242295 times days,
  vz -0.0000951592254519715870 times days and mass 0.0000515138902046611451 times sunmass to bodies.

to find the energy of some bodies
  set e to 0.0.
  set n to the number of items in the bodies.
  for every i from 1 to n
    set b to item i of the bodies.
    add 0.5 times the mass of b times (the vx of b squared plus the vy of b squared plus the vz of b squared) to e.
    for every j from i plus 1 to n
      set c to item j of the bodies.
      set dx to the x of b minus the x of c.
      set dy to the y of b minus the y of c.
      set dz to the z of b minus the z of c.
      subtract the mass of b times the mass of c divided by the square root of (dx squared plus dy squared plus dz squared) from e.
    that's all.
  that's all.
  give back e.
that's all.

to advance some bodies by some dt
  set n to the number of items in the bodies.
  for every i from 1 to n
    set b to item i of the bodies.
    for every j from i plus 1 to n
      set c to item j of the bodies.
      set dx to the x of b minus the x of c.
      set dy to the y of b minus the y of c.
      set dz to the z of b minus the z of c.
      set d2 to dx squared plus dy squared plus dz squared.
      set mag to dt divided by (d2 times the square root of d2).
      set mb to the mass of b times mag.
      set mc to the mass of c times mag.
      subtract dx times mc from the vx of b.
      subtract dy times mc from the vy of b.
      subtract dz times mc from the vz of b.
      add dx times mb to the vx of c.
      add dy times mb to the vy of c.
      add dz times mb to the vz of c.
    that's all.
  that's all.
  for every b in the bodies
    add dt times the vx of b to the x of b.
    add dt times the vy of b to the y of b.
    add dt times the vz of b to the z of b.
  that's all.
that's all.

set px to 0.0.
set py to 0.0.
set pz to 0.0.
for every b in bodies
  add the vx of b times the mass of b to px.
  add the vy of b times the mass of b to py.
  add the vz of b times the mass of b to pz.
that's all.
set sun to item 1 of bodies.
set the vx of sun to 0.0 minus (px divided by sunmass).
set the vy of sun to 0.0 minus (py divided by sunmass).
set the vz of sun to 0.0 minus (pz divided by sunmass).

say the energy of bodies with 9 decimals.
repeat 5000000 times, advance bodies by 0.01.
say the energy of bodies with 9 decimals.
